+### Compound Durations
+
+`parseCompound` sums several `<number><unit>` pieces. Pieces can be separated by whitespace, a comma, or nothing at all.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+```
+
+It throws a `TypeError` if any piece can't be parsed. A bare number (no unit) is only accepted on its own, e.g. `parseCompound('100')`.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
